-- title:
--   Parabolic Hecke eigenclasses and points of the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ be a natural number, $S$ a set of natural numbers, and $F$ a field of characteristic zero. Write $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M ⊤`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ obtained by pulling the full subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ back along [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) and pushing into $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, and let $H^1(M,A) = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma, A)$ denote the additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma$ (written additively) to an abelian group $A$; for a prime $\ell$ the operator [`CohCarrier.heckeT M ⊤ ℓ A`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) on $H^1(M,A)$ is the transfer of the restriction of a homomorphism along the conjugation map [`CohCarrier.conjL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L228). Let $c \in H^1(M,F)$ be nonzero and parabolic, i.e. $c(\gamma)=0$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$ whose matrix satisfies $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$, and let $a : \mathbb N \to F$ be such that `heckeT` at every prime $\ell \notin S$ acts on $c$ by the scalar $a(\ell)$. Let $\mathbb T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` at primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ and `heckeULin` at primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\chi : \mathbb T \to F$ with $\chi(T_\ell) = a(\ell)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, and $\chi(U_q) = a(q)$ for all primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$, and such that for every field $K$ of characteristic zero and every ring homomorphism $\psi : \mathbb T \to K$ with $\chi(t) = 0 \iff \psi(t) = 0$ for all $t$, there exists a nonzero parabolic $c' \in H^1(M,K)$ on which `heckeT` at each prime $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ acts by the scalar $\psi(T_\ell)$ and at each prime $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$ by the scalar $\psi(U_q)$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura passage from a parabolic Hecke eigenclass to an $F$-valued point of the weight-two cuspidal Hecke algebra, together with the rationality statement that such an eigenclass exists over any characteristic-zero field receiving a homomorphism with the same kernel. It is used in the project's construction of Galois-theoretic data attached to Hecke eigensystems, notably in the results identifying the residue of $U_q$ with a Frobenius trace and in the passage from points of the Hecke algebra to eigenclasses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_and_forall_exists_eigenclass_of_ker_eq.lean

